content.text:
Here's a complete memory matching game built with plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. It includes eight pairs, a move counter, and a reshuffle button.
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
<title>Memory Match</title>
<style>
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    min-height: 100vh;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    padding: clamp(12px, 4vw, 28px);
    font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    color: #e8eef7;
    background:
      radial-gradient(1200px 600px at 15% -10%, #1d2c46 0%, transparent 60%),
      radial-gradient(900px 500px at 110% 110%, #2a1b3d 0%, transparent 55%),
      #080c12;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }

  .app {
    width: min(100%, 520px);
    padding: clamp(16px, 4vw, 24px);
    border-radius: 22px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.045);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.09);
    box-shadow: 0 30px 70px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
  }

  /* ---------- Header ---------- */
  .top {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #cfe4f5;
  }

  .stats { display: flex; gap: 8px; }

  .stat {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 6px 11px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: rgba(110, 231, 255, 0.08);
    border: 1px solid rgba(110, 231, 255, 0.22);
    color: #a9d8e8;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .stat b {
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-left: 4px;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  /* ---------- Board ---------- */
  .board {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(7px, 2vw, 11px);
  }

  .card {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    min-width: 0;
    perspective: 800px;
    cursor: pointer;
    border-radius: 14px;
    transition: transform 0.18s ease;
    -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
  }

  .card:not(.is-flipped):not(.is-matched):hover { transform: translateY(-4px); }
  .card:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #6ee7ff; outline-offset: 3px; }

  .card-inner {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;
    transition: transform 0.45s cubic-bezier(0.22, 0.75, 0.3, 1);
    border-radius: 14px;
  }

  .card.is-flipped .card-inner,
  .card.is-matched .card-inner { transform: rotateY(180deg); }

  .card-face {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border-radius: 14px;
    backface-visibility: hidden;
    -webkit-backface-visibility: hidden;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 7vw, 2.3rem);
    line-height: 1;
    user-select: none;
  }

  /* Face-down side */
  .card-front {
    background: linear-gradient(155deg, #31435f, #1a2331 65%);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    color: rgba(160, 215, 240, 0.55);
    font-size: clamp(0.95rem, 3.4vw, 1.15rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1), inset 0 -6px 14px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
  }

  .card-front::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 7px;
    border-radius: 9px;
    border: 1px dashed rgba(190, 230, 255, 0.18);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* Face-up side */
  .card-back {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
    background: linear-gradient(155deg, #ffffff, #dbe7f6);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
    box-shadow: inset 0 -3px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06), 0 6px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);
  }

  .card.is-matched { cursor: default; animation: pop 0.4s ease; }
  .card.is-matched .card-back {
    background: linear-gradient(155deg, #ddfff0, #9ff0cd);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.55), 0 0 20px rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.35);
  }

  @keyframes pop {
    0%   { transform: scale(1); }
    45%  { transform: scale(1.07); }
    100% { transform: scale(1); }
  }

  /* ---------- Message + button ---------- */
  .message {
    min-height: 1.4em;
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: #9fb3c8;
  }

  .message.win {
    color: #a7f3d0;
    font-weight: 700;
    animation: fade 0.4s ease both;
  }

  @keyframes fade { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(4px); } }

  .reshuffle {
    margin-top: 14px;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 12px 18px;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 12px;
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: #06121a;
    cursor: pointer;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6ee7ff, #a78bfa);
    transition: transform 0.15s ease, filter 0.15s ease;
  }

  .reshuffle:hover { filter: brightness(1.08); }
  .reshuffle:active { transform: scale(0.98); }
  .reshuffle:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #fff; outline-offset: 3px; }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .card, .card-inner { transition: none; }
    .card.is-matched { animation: none; }
    .message.win { animation: none; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

  <main class="app">
    <div class="top">
      <h1>Memory Match</h1>
      <div class="stats">
        <span class="stat">Moves <b id="moves">0</b></span>
        <span class="stat">Pairs <b id="pairs">0 / 8</b></span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="board" class="board" aria-label="Memory card board"></div>

    <p id="message" class="message" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

    <button id="reshuffle" class="reshuffle" type="button">Reshuffle</button>
  </main>

<script>
(function () {
  "use strict";

  const SYMBOLS = ["🍕", "🚀", "🐙", "🌵", "🎈", "🎧", "🍄", "⚡"];
  const PAIR_COUNT = SYMBOLS.length;

  const boardEl     = document.getElementById("board");
  const movesEl     = document.getElementById("moves");
  const pairsEl     = document.getElementById("pairs");
  const messageEl   = document.getElementById("message");
  const reshuffleEl = document.getElementById("reshuffle");

  let firstCard   = null;   // first flipped card of the current turn
  let lockBoard   = false;  // true while a mismatch is being shown
  let moves       = 0;
  let matchedPairs = 0;
  let gameToken   = 0;      // invalidates pending timers after a reshuffle

  /* ---------- Helpers ---------- */

  function shuffle(array) {
    for (let i = array.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {
      const j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));
      [array[i], array[j]] = [array[j], array[i]];
    }
    return array;
  }

  function makeCard(symbol) {
    const card = document.createElement("button");
    card.type = "button";
    card.className = "card";
    card.dataset.symbol = symbol;
    card.setAttribute("aria-label", "Face-down card");

    const inner = document.createElement("span");
    inner.className = "card-inner";

    const front = document.createElement("span");
    front.className = "card-face card-front";
    front.textContent = "?";

    const back = document.createElement("span");
    back.className = "card-face card-back";
    back.textContent = symbol;

    inner.append(front, back);
    card.append(inner);
    card.addEventListener("click", () => flip(card));
    return card;
  }

  /* ---------- Game setup ---------- */

  function startGame() {
    gameToken++;
    firstCard = null;
    lockBoard = false;
    moves = 0;
    matchedPairs = 0;

    movesEl.textContent = "0";
    pairsEl.textContent = "0 / " + PAIR_COUNT;
    messageEl.textContent = "";
    messageEl.classList.remove("win");

    // 8 symbols × 2 = 16 cards, shuffled
    const deck = shuffle(SYMBOLS.flatMap((symbol) => [symbol, symbol]));

    const fragment = document.createDocumentFragment();
    deck.forEach((symbol) => fragment.append(makeCard(symbol)));
    boardEl.replaceChildren(fragment);
  }

  /* ---------- Turn logic ---------- */

  function flip(card) {
    if (lockBoard) return;
    if (card.classList.contains("is-flipped") || card.classList.contains("is-matched")) return;

    card.classList.add("is-flipped");
    card.setAttribute("aria-label", "Card showing " + card.dataset.symbol);

    // First card of the turn
    if (!firstCard) {
      firstCard = card;
      return;
    }

    // Second card of the turn
    const second = card;
    moves++;
    movesEl.textContent = moves;

    // ---- Match ----
    if (firstCard.dataset.symbol === second.dataset.symbol) {
      const a = firstCard;
      const b = second;
      firstCard = null;

      a.classList.add("is-matched");
      b.classList.add("is-matched");
      a.setAttribute("aria-label", "Card showing " + a.dataset.symbol + ", matched");
      b.setAttribute("aria-label", "Card showing " + b.dataset.symbol + ", matched");

      matchedPairs++;
      pairsEl.textContent = matchedPairs + " / " + PAIR_COUNT;

      if (matchedPairs === PAIR_COUNT) {
        messageEl.textContent =
          "🎉 You found all " + PAIR_COUNT + " pairs in " + moves + " " +
          (moves === 1 ? "move" : "moves") + "!";
        messageEl.classList.add("win");
      }
      return;
    }

    // ---- Mismatch: show both briefly, then flip back ----
    const a = firstCard;
    const b = second;
    const token = gameToken;
    firstCard = null;
    lockBoard = true;

    setTimeout(() => {
      if (token !== gameToken) return; // board was reshuffled in the meantime
      a.classList.remove("is-flipped");
      b.classList.remove("is-flipped");
      a.setAttribute("aria-label", "Face-down card");
      b.setAttribute("aria-label", "Face-down card");
      lockBoard = false;
    }, 850);
  }

  /* ---------- Wiring ---------- */

  reshuffleEl.addEventListener("click", startGame);

  startGame();
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
```
### Gameplay & Interaction

You flip two cards per turn, and matched pairs stay face up while mismatches flip back after a short delay.

- **Turn flow:** Each click reveals a card. When two are facing up, the game compares their symbols. A match locks them in place; a mismatch briefly shows both before flipping back.
- **Counters & feedback:** The move counter increments for every pair attempt, and the pairs counter tracks progress. A win message appears once all eight pairs are found, announced via the live region for screen readers.
- **Reshuffle & reset:** The button reshuffles the deck, clears the board, and resets everything — including pending mismatch timers through a token system so old timeouts don't interfere.
- **Accessibility & motion:** Cards are real buttons with dynamic aria-labels, keyboard focus is visible, and reduced-motion preferences disable the flip and pop animations.
---

**Optimization Tip:** You can customize the card symbols by editing the `SYMBOLS` array near the top of the script. To change how long mismatched cards stay visible, adjust the `850` millisecond delay in the `setTimeout` call.

